              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scott Pallo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Freaking Awesome. These are simple, easy, and maybe the best recipe on the website. I seldom make recipes without significantly more reviews and am extremely happy I tried this one. Good by themselves and with the sauce. do yourself a favor...make these and don't screw with the ingredients. I will never make regular crab cakes again after these bad boys. ( First review ever because they deserved it )"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gderr the dysfunctional"
            },
            "reviewBody": "changes---low fat mayo and low fat sour cream. doubled the horseradish, used 1 teaspoon crushed garlic and doubled the lemon. this combo got our noses running. we managed to catch 'em, but I will scale back next time. I rolled the crab mixture into balls then flatten 'em after browning on one side. these make PLENTY! so be careful if you want a dinner for 2. I halved the recipe and there was @ 18 nice 'uns. don't get me wrong this is a GREAT recipe. I used zatarians hush-puppy mix. oops, sauted scallions before adding to batter. this is really good stuff! I don't understand why more folks haven't tried this....",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-03T20:27:05.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "DREGINEK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made 4/21/25. The garlic sauce of this is FANTASTIC and 5 stars. It made a lot so we used leftovers for a steak meal later that week. The crab fritters? Only okay-good. Good! But not overly impressive to us. Used canned crab claw meat (which is expensive!) and instead of hush puppy mix, used Bisquick…..and a little more of it after I dropped the first fritter in the oil and it spread out like a pancake. This makes a lot but unfortunately leftovers do not reheat well. I’m glad we tried (and will make this garlic sauce again!!) Thanks FoodieGeek!",
            "datePublished": "2025-04-27T19:44:35.944Z"
          },
